   "text": "The drawing matches travoprost, the isopropyl ester of a prostaglandin F2\u03b1 analogue. I wrote the SMILES from the structure, but I took the stereodescriptors from the known stereochemistry of travoprost rather than re-deriving each wedge and hash from the image.\n\n- **Ester end:** an isopropyl group on the ester oxygen, then the carbonyl.\n- **Upper chain:** three CH2 groups, then a cis (Z) C=C, then one more CH2 that joins the cyclopentane through a hashed bond. This gives the hept-5-enoate chain.\n- **Cyclopentane:** two ring OH groups, drawn with hashed bonds, and a ring CH2 between them.\n- **Lower chain:** a trans (E) CH=CH attached to the ring by a wedged bond. Next comes a CH(OH) with a hashed bond, then CH2\u2013O\u2013aryl.\n- **Aryl group:** a benzene ring bearing CF3 meta to the ether oxygen.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)OC(=O)CCC/C=C\\C[C@H]1[C@H](C[C@H]([C@@H]1/C=C/[C@H](COC2=CC=CC(=C2)C(F)(F)F)O)O)O"
